"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproduces in 4.6\nDoes not reproduce in 4.5\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7216) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K (32 threads) - 63.78 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nJust did an import of my project and now all my ViewportTextures are broken.\n\n<img width=\"742\" height=\"684\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/45aed91b-53ec-4795-9ee1-af099c0485d9\" />\n\nThis is a visual shader that uses a viewport texture passed into a Texture2DParameter. Recreating the ViewportTexture fixes the problem, but only while the file is open. The next time the tscn is loaded, the viewport is not longer rendered.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen a 4.5 project that uses viewport textures in 4.6\nResult: ViewportTexture is magenta.\nExpected: should show contents of viewport\n\nClear the viewport texture and reassign to a new viewport texture that points at the subviewport\nResults: viewport texture now renders correctly\n\nSave scene and reload.\nResults: Texture is back to being magenta.\nExpected: Texture should load and display viewport frames.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nn/a","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.